      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: the event review remains incomplete\n\nI confirmed the requested work order and the Pending Close cutoff, but **the records I’m authorized to read contain no cost-event rows**. I therefore cannot establish whether an event was created after that cutoff.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, DeKoven — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** — no timezone supplied |\n| Source transaction | Not available in authorized records |\n| Event amount | Not available |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event evidence |\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before the cutoff continue to be processed. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nThus, for a non-exempt transaction created after this cutoff, a held/unprocessed status would be consistent with the documented treatment; a processed/accounted status would not. That is a conditional policy assessment—not a finding about this work order’s event.\n\nThe supporting event records are restricted to the records-custodian role. I requested an authorized extract and escalated the evidence gap without accessing restricted copies. **No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_f1a3752d2e06/audit-report.json`; the submitted report is marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
